# Consumable production Compose environment-removal approvals.
# Format: service|destination_key|source_variable|exact_default
#
# Keep this file empty during normal operation. To retire a mapping, deploy an
# approval-only release first. The immediately following release must either
# remove the exact mapping or revoke the approval, and must remove the approval
# in both cases. If current has any active record, candidate must have no active
# records: an approval cannot survive, be replaced, or be combined with a new
# approval. A newly staged mapping must already exist unchanged in current and
# candidate Compose. The active release, never the candidate, authorizes the
# transition. This file must remain a regular non-executable Git blob (100644).
# The byte contract is printable ASCII with LF or paired CRLF line endings,
# bounded to 65536 bytes. Tabs, lone CR, NUL and other binary/control bytes are
# rejected before Bash parsing. Comments must start in column 1, and blank lines
# must be exactly empty. The fourth field may be empty only to represent the
# exact Compose form ${VARIABLE:-}; it is never written to logs or records.
